  "intro": "The Text Case Converter takes one block of text and renders 15 case formats side by side — uppercase, lowercase, sentence case, Title Case, Headline Case, camelCase, PascalCase, CONSTANT_CASE, snake_case, kebab-case, slug-case, dot.case, path/case, Inverse Case and Alternating Case. It works by splitting your input on every run of non-alphanumeric characters (the regex /[^A-Za-z0-9]+/) into a clean word list, then rejoining those words with the separator and capitalisation each format requires; the uppercase and lowercase cards apply JavaScript's native toUpperCase() and toLowerCase() to the raw string instead, so punctuation and spacing survive intact. Headline Case follows an AP-style list of 19 short words that stay lowercase unless they open or close the line, while sentence case lowercases everything and then re-capitalises the first word character and anything following a period, question mark or exclamation mark. Every conversion is recomputed in a React useMemo inside your own browser as you type — the tool makes no network requests, so the text you paste is never uploaded.",
