      "Can I wear shorts at temples in Thailand?",
      "Not inside the halls. Ordinary wats expect shoulders and knees covered, and you remove your shoes before entering the ordination or image hall. A sarong carried in a day bag wraps over shorts in seconds, which is why most travellers pack one whatever else they bring."
